'''Space-Time Smackdown''' (Japanese: '''{{j|時空の激闘}}''' ''Intense Fight of Space and Time'') is the second main expansion of cards in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

== Information ==
'''Space-Time Smackdown''' is the second main expansion released through [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. The expansion focuses heavily on [[Generation IV]], with many of its cards featuring Pokémon, characters, and locations from the [[Sinnoh]] region. It also sees the introduction of {{TCG|Pokémon Tool}} cards to the game, as well as the {{TCG|Burned}} and {{TCG|Confused}} {{TCG|Special Condition}}s. Its two booster packs are themed around {{p|Dialga}} and {{p|Palkia}}, the [[game mascot]]s and featured [[Legendary Pokémon]] of {{game|Diamond and Pearl|s}}—and their remakes, {{g|Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl}}—respectively.

Its Japanese name is an amalgamation of the first and final Pokémon Card Game DP expansions in Japan, {{TCG|Space-Time Creation}} ('''{{j|時空の創造}}''') and {{TCG|Intense Fight in the Destroyed Sky}} ('''{{j|破空の激闘}}'''), which were released internationally as {{TCG|Diamond & Pearl}} and {{TCG|Stormfront}}.

Several of the [[#Themed Collections|Themed Collections]] made available alongside Space-Time Smackdown also reference elements of Sinnoh and the Generation IV games:
* '''Legends of [[Newmoon Island]] and [[Fullmoon Island]]''' feature the islands' inhabitants, {{p|Darkrai}} and {{p|Cresselia}} respectively;
* '''Giants Unleashed''' features {{p|Regigigas}} and the [[legendary giants]], all of which feature artwork which may depict [[Snowpoint Temple]];
* '''Battle with Champion Cynthia''' features [[Cynthia]] and the five Generation IV Pokémon on her champion battle team;
* '''Ecosystem of Stark Mountain''' features {{p|Heatran}} and other Pokémon that can be found in [[Stark Mountain]], all of which feature artwork depicting it;
* '''New Discoveries of the Sinnoh Region''' features 21 Pokémon that evolve from Pokémon introduced prior to Generation IV;
* '''Team Galactic, Assemble!''' features [[Cyrus]] and other [[Team Galactic]] members alongside some of their commonly used Pokémon.

Additionally, two further Themed Collections make reference to {{game|Platinum}}, a follow-up and [[upper version]] to Diamond and Pearl:
* '''Unknown Distortion World''' features {{p|Giratina}} in its Origin Forme alongside [[lake guardians]] {{p|Uxie}}, {{p|Mesprit}}, and {{p|Azelf}}, refering their expanded story role in Platinum and the introduction of Giratina's Origin Forme;
* '''Mischievous Shapeshifters''' features {{p|Rotom}} in its various forms, which were first introduced in Platinum following Rotom's introduction in Diamond and Pearl.

